<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Crater Peak</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:312-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="42.896827" lon="-122.133714"><ele>1973.4</ele><name>Park Headquarters parking</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:crater-lake-park-headquarters (as in 311-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6475; quote: From the parking area at Park Headquarters (6,475 feet) ski east 1.7 miles to the trail's high point</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.880130" lon="-122.116930"><ele>2069.4</ele><name>Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive)</name><desc>source: copied from 311-1: OSM East Rim Drive node 40187236; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6806; quote: ski east 1.7 miles to the trail's high point after an initial descent then the long climb of over 400 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.876608" lon="-122.104271"><ele>2032.2</ele><name>Crater Peak Trail turn (Rim Drive)</name><desc>source: OSM Rim Drive node 40187284, 2.4 mi from the pin, 62 m from the Crater Peak Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 313; book_elev_ft: 6654; quote: Continue on the Rim Road 0.7 mile to Crater Peak Trail, which goes off to the south</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.876176" lon="-122.103778"><ele>2028.3</ele><name>Crater Peak Trail at the rim-road bend</name><desc>source: OSM Crater Peak Trail way 652150449 node nearest the Rim Drive (DEM 6,655 ft, the map's 6654'); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 314; book_elev_ft: 6654; quote: the marked route turns south off the Rim Road ... following an old road 1 mile downhill to Tutuni Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="42.848182" lon="-122.097225"><ele>2213.4</ele><name>Crater Peak summit (rim high point)</name><desc>source: OSM Crater Peak Trail's highest node on the crater rim (DEM 7,262 ft); GNIS-style peak node 357308420 is 47 m west; confidence: high; pdf_page: 314; book_elev_ft: 7265; quote: This high cinder cone at 7,265 feet ... up a very steep 765 feet to the summit crater rim</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Crater Peak</name><desc>1. Park Headquarters parking -&gt; Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive): osm (high), 1.81 mi | 2. Sun Notch Trail high point (East Rim Drive) -&gt; Crater Peak Trail turn (Rim Drive): osm (high), 0.73 mi | 3. Crater Peak Trail turn (Rim Drive) -&gt; Crater Peak Trail at the rim-road bend: straight (medium), 0.04 mi | 4. Crater Peak Trail at the rim-road bend -&gt; Crater Peak summit (rim high point): osm (medium), 2.62 mi</desc>
